1. the full form, no exception
   begin body runs
   begin body finished
   else runs: no exception was raised
   ensure runs
2. the full form, an exception
   begin body runs
   rescue runs: ZeroDivisionError: divided by 0
   ensure runs
3. rescue A, B => e catches either class, and their subclasses
   caught ZeroDivisionError, which is_a?(IndexError): false
   caught IndexError, which is_a?(IndexError): true
   caught KeyError, which is_a?(IndexError): true
4. retry re-runs the begin body
   attempt 1
   attempt 2
   attempt 3
   succeeded on attempt 3
5. ensure runs on return
   ensure ran on the way out
   method returned "the return value"
6. return inside ensure swallows the exception (never do this)
   method returned "ensure's return value"; no exception reached the caller
7. rescue in a def needs no begin
   parse("12")  -> 12
   parse("abc") -> "rescued ArgumentError"
8. what the rescued object carries
   e.class            ZeroDivisionError
   e.message          "divided by 0"
   e.backtrace        an Array of Strings
   e.full_message     a String (paths inside, not printed)
9. begin/end is an expression
   body raised, rescue ran:     "the rescue clause's value"
   body ok, else and ensure ran: 3 (ensure's 4 is discarded)
